	"web_text": "Although Red, Yellow, Blue has a clear relationship to Folsom Street Variations III (see 1991.28.665), Diebenkorn rendered the former with a softer composition than the latter, incorporating a subtle curvilinear arch to frame multiple intersecting triangles. A dusty-pink outline adds further warmth to the composition, while the dense scribbly etched lines, which cover the blue sections, lend texture and depth.",
